If we circumscribe a square around our ellipse, then slopes of the tangent lines (i.e. $ y'$ ) shall equal either equal 1 (2nd & 4th quadrants) or -1 (1st & 3rd quadrants).  Squaring (ii) will yield: $1 = \frac{b^2x^2}{a^2(a^2 - x^2)}$ ;

