Note that  $$   \sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\sum_{m=1}^{\infty} \frac{1}{m^2 n +m n^2 +2mn }= \sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\sum_{m=1}^{\infty} \frac{1}{mn(m+n+2) }
=\sum_{k=2}^{\infty}\sum_{m=1}^{k-1} \frac{1}{m(k-m)(k+2)} $$    $$ =\sum_{k=2}^{\infty}\frac{1}{(k+2)k}\sum_{m=1}^{k-1} \frac{k}{m(k-m)}=\sum_{k=2}^{\infty}\frac{1}{(k+2)k}\left (\sum_{m=1}^{k-1} \frac{1}{n}+\frac{1}{k-n}  \right ) $$    $$ =\sum_{k=2}^{\infty}\frac{2H_{k-1}}{(k+2)k}=\sum_{k=2}^{\infty}H_{k-1}\left ( \frac{1}{k}-\frac{1}{k+2} \right )=\sum_{k=2}^{\infty}H_{k-1}\left ( \frac{1}{k}-\frac{1}{k+2} \right )=\sum_{k=2}^{\infty}\frac{H_{k-1}}{k}-\frac{H_{k+1}}{k+2}+\frac{1}{k(k+2)}+\frac{1}{(k+1)(k+2)} $$    $$ =\frac{H_1}{2}+\frac{H_2}{3}+\frac 12\sum_{k=2}^{\infty}\frac{1}{k}-\frac{1}{k+2}+\sum_{k=2}^{\infty}\frac{1}{(k+1)}-\frac{1}{(k+2)}=1+\frac{5}{12}+\frac{1}{3}=\frac{7}{4} $$  Regards
Claudio.

