Alternative solution: Notice that  $\sin x \sin x^2=\frac{1}{2}\text{Re} \left( e^{-ix+ix^2}-e^{ix+ix^2} \right)$ . Now, 
\begin{align*}
    \left|\int_0^\infty e^{-ix+ix^2}-e^{ix+ix^2}dx \right|&= \left|e^{-\frac{i}{4}}\int_0^\infty e^{i\left(x-\frac{1}{2}\right)^2}-e^{i\left(x+\frac{1}{2}\right)^2}dx\right|= \left|\int_{-\frac{1}{2}}^\infty e^{iy^2}dy-\int_{\frac{1}{2}}^\infty e^{iy^2}dy\right|= \left|\int_{-\frac{1}{2}}^{\frac{1}{2}}e^{iy^2}dy\right|
    &\leq \int_{-\frac{1}{2}}^{\frac{1}{2}}\left|e^{iy^2}\right|dy=1
\end{align*}
Therefore  $\left|\int_0^\infty \sin x \sin x^2 dx\right|\leq\frac{1}{2}\left|\int_0^\infty e^{-ix+ix^2}-e^{ix+ix^2}dx \right|\leq\frac{1}{2}$

