Let  $h(x)=a_nx^n+a_{n-1}x^{n-1}+\cdots+a_1x+a_0$ .
Assume FTSOC that for some distinct  $a,b \in \{0,1,\ldots,p^3-1\}$  the congruence  $h(a) \equiv h(b) \pmod{p^3}$ . Then they must be congruent  $\pmod{p^2}$ , which using the condition implies that  $p^2 \mid a-b$ . Thus WLOG  $a<b$  and write  $b=kp^2+a$ , where  $1\leq k<p$ . Now note that by the binomial theorem:  $$ (kp^2+a)^r-a^r \equiv akrp^2 \pmod{p^3}, $$  since any other coefficients are  $0 \pmod{p}$ . Thus for  $h(a) \equiv h(b) \pmod{p^3}$ , it is necessary to have:
\begin{align*}
\sum_{i=1}^n a_i((kp^2+a)^i-a^i) &\equiv 0 \pmod{p^3}
ak\sum_{i=1}^n ia_ip^2 &\equiv 0 \pmod{p^3}
ak\sum_{i=1}^n ia_i &\equiv 0 \pmod{p}.
\end{align*}
Now consider  $h(a)$  and  $h(kp+a)$ . Note that:  $$ (kp+a)^r-a^r \equiv akrp \pmod{p^2}. $$  Now by the condition, these must be distinct  $\pmod{p^2}$ , or:
\begin{align*}
\sum_{i=1}^n a_i((kp+a)^i-a^i) &\not \equiv 0 \pmod{p^2}
ak\sum_{i=1}^n ia_ip &\not\equiv 0 \pmod{p^2}
ak\sum_{i=1}^n ia_i &\not\equiv 0 \pmod{p}.
\end{align*}
Which is a contradiction.  $\blacksquare$

