\begin{align*}
p(2019)&=\sum_{n=0}^{1008} F_{2n+1} \prod_{\substack{j=0 j\ne n}}^{1008} \frac{2019-(2j+1)}{(2n+1)-(2j+1)} \tag{Lagrange, see comments}
&=\sum_{n=0}^{1008} F_{2n+1} \prod_{\substack{j=0 j\ne n}}^{1008} \frac{1009-j}{n-j}
&=\sum_{n=0}^{1008} F_{2n+1} (-1)^{1008-n}\binom{1009}{n}
&=\sum_{n=0}^{1008} [x^{2n+1}]\frac{x}{1-x-x^2} (-1)^{1008-n}\binom{1009}{n}
&=[x^{2019}]\sum_{n=0}^{1008} x^{2019-2n-1}\frac{x}{1-x-x^2} (-1)^{1008-n}\binom{1009}{n} \tag{*}
&=[x^{2019}]\frac{x^{2019}}{1-x-x^2}\sum_{n=0}^{1008} \left(\frac{1}{x^2}\right)^{n} (-1)^{1008-n}\binom{1009}{n}
&=[x^{2019}]\frac{x^{2019}}{1-x-x^2}\left(\left(\frac{1}{x^2}\right)^{1009} - \left(\frac{1}{x^2}-1\right)^{1009} \right)
&=[x^{2019}]\frac{x}{1-x-x^2}-[x^{2019}]\frac{x}{1-x-x^2}(1-x^2)^{1009}
&=F_{2019}-[x^{2019}]\frac{x}{1-x-x^2}(x+1-x-x^2)^{1009}
&=F_{2019}-[x^{2019}]\frac{x}{1-x-x^2}\sum_{n=0}^{1009}\binom{1009}{n}(1-x-x^2)^n x^{1009-n}
&=F_{2019}-F_{1010} \tag{**}
\end{align*}
To understand  $\textrm{(*)}$  note that multiplying a polynomial by a power of  $x$  will move any coefficients you were tracking to a different power of  $x$ .  All of the desired coefficients are aligned to  $x^{2019}$ .


To understand  $\textrm{(**)}$  note that only the first term of the sum leads to an expression with a quadratic denominator and hence a power series.  All other terms of the sum lead to expressions which are polynomials rather than power series with degrees less than  $2019$  hence they make no contribution to the coefficient of  $x^{2019}$ .


