From the above claim, we see that  $P_n$  is isomorphic to the ``flower of order  $n$ '', which is an inductively defined set of points of size  $4n+5$ , where at each step, a new square is added that circumscribes the previous construction. It's hard to describe this exactly in words, but here's a picture of the flower of order  $7$ , which should make it clear what the construction is. [asy]
draw((1,0)--(0,1)--(-1,0)--(0,-1)--cycle,dotted);
draw((1,1)--(-1,1)--(-1,-1)--(1,-1)--cycle);
draw((2,0)--(0,2)--(-2,0)--(0,-2)--cycle,dotted);
draw((2,2)--(-2,2)--(-2,-2)--(2,-2)--cycle);
draw((4,0)--(0,4)--(-4,0)--(0,-4)--cycle,dotted);
draw((4,4)--(-4,4)--(-4,-4)--(4,-4)--cycle);
