The odd power sum follows from the problem's condition, while the even power sums are trivially equal because  $x^{2k} = (-x)^{2k}$ . Thus, we obtain that these two sequences must be permutations of each other. In particular,  $-1$  must be somewhere in the second sequence, implying that  $x_i\in\{-1,1\}$  for some  $i$ , a contradiction.</details>

