Consider  $f(a, b, c) = \frac{a}{b + c + 1} + \frac{b}{c + a + 1} + \frac{c}{b + c + 1} + (1 - a)(1 - b)(1 - c)$ . Then we have that 

\begin{align*}
\frac{\partial^2f}{\partial a^2} &= \frac{\partial}{\partial a} \left(\frac{1}{b + c + 1} - \left(\frac{b}{(c + a + 1)^2} + \frac{c}{(a + b + 1)^2} \right) + (b - 1)(1 - c) \right) 
&= \frac{2b}{(c + a + 1)^2} + \frac{2c}{(a + b + 1)^2} 
&\geq 0 \text{ over } [0, 1]
\end{align*}
Hence we have that the  $f$  attains it's maximum for  $a, b, c = 0, 1$ . Now checking that  $f \leq 1$  for all  $a, b, c = 0, 1$  is trivial, and we are done.  $\blacksquare$

