Then :
\begin{align*}
OM_k &= 1/\cos k^\circ 
\text{m} \angle M_a O M_b &= (b-a)^\circ 
[M_a O M_b ] &= \tfrac{1}{2} \sin (b-a)^\circ \cdot OM_a \cdot OM_b =
\frac{\tfrac{1}{2} \sin (b-a)^\circ}{\cos a^\circ \cos b^\circ} ,
\end{align*}
so
\begin{align*} \sum_{k=0}^{88} \frac{\tfrac{1}{2} \sin 1^{\circ}}{\cos k^\circ \cos (k+1)^\circ} &= \sum_{k=0}^{88} [M_k O M_{k+1} ] 
&= [M_0 O M_{89} ] = \frac{\tfrac{1}{2} \sin 89^\circ}{ \cos 0^\circ \cos 89^\circ} = \frac{\tfrac{1}{2} \cos 1^\circ}{\sin 1^\circ}, 
\end{align*}
which proves the desired identity.

