Take a homothety of ratio  $\frac 12$  centered at  $E$  taking  $E_1E_2E_3E_4$  to  $E_1'E_2'E_3'E_4'$ . It suffices to prove that  $E_1', E_2', E_3', E_4'$  are concyclic. Angle chasing suffices: 
\begin{align*}
\measuredangle E_4'E_3'E_2' &= \measuredangle E_4'E_3'E+\measuredangle EE_3'E_2'  
&= \measuredangle E_4'DE + \measuredangle ECE_2' 
&= 90^{\circ} - \measuredangle DEE_4'+90^{\circ} - \measuredangle E_2'EC 
&= -(\measuredangle DEE_4 + \measuredangle E_2'EC), 
\end{align*}
and
\begin{align*} 
\measuredangle E_4'E_1'E_2' &= \measuredangle E_4'E_1'E+\measuredangle EE_1'E_2 
&= \measuredangle E_4'AE + \measuredangle EBE_2' 
&= 90^{\circ} - \measuredangle AEE_4' + 90^{\circ} - \measuredangle E_2'EB 
&= -(\measuredangle AEE_4'+\measuredangle E_2'EB). 
\end{align*} But   $$ \measuredangle DEE_4'+\measuredangle E_2'EC - (\measuredangle AEE_4'-\measuredangle E_2'EB) = \measuredangle DEE_4'+\measuredangle E_2'EC + \measuredangle E_4'EA + \measuredangle BEE_2' = 0, $$   which gives   $$ \measuredangle DEE_4' + \measuredangle E_2'EC = \measuredangle AEE_4' + \measuredangle E_2'EB \implies \measuredangle E_4'E_3'E_2' = \measuredangle E_4'E_1'E_2' $$   tells us that  $E_1', E_2', E_3', E_4'$  are concyclic. Therefore,  $E_1, E_2, E_3, E_4$  are concyclic as desired.

