\[ \angle{PEH}=\angle{PDH}=\angle{ADB}=\angle{ACB}=\angle{PCF}=\angle{PEF}. \quad \blacksquare\]

<span style="color:blue">**Claim 2.**</span>  $\angle{HEP}+\angle{PGH}=90^\circ$ *Proof.* Like in Claim 1, we know that  $\angle{HEP}=\angle{PEH}=\angle{ACB}=\angle{PCB}$ . Furthermore we know
\[ \angle{PGH}=\angle{PAH}=\angle{CAD}=\angle{CBD}=\angle{PBC}. \]
Because  $\angle{CPB}=90^\circ$  because the diagonals of  $ABCD$  are perpendicular, we are done.  $\blacksquare$ This implies that  $EFGH$  is cyclic because if we combine Claim 1 and Claim 2, we get that  $\angle{HEF}+\angle{HGF}=180^\circ$  or that it is cyclic.  $\blacksquare$

Denote by  $X,Y,Z,W$  the foot of perpendiculars from  $AB,AD,DC,BC$  respectively. 
