Now we note that the quadrilaterals  $AXEY, BWEX,WCZE, YEZD$  are all cyclic quadrilaterals, so we get the following \begin{align*}
\angle XWE + \angle  XYE &= \angle XBE + \angle XAE = 90^{\circ}  
\angle EYZ + \angle EWZ &= \angle EDZ + \angle ECZ = 90^{\circ}
\end{align*} 
Hence we see that \[\angle XWE = \angle XYE = \angle EYZ + \angle EWZ = \angle XYZ + \angle XWZ = 180^{\circ} \] which proves that the quadrilateral  $XYZW$  is a cyclic quadrilateral, giving us the desired result.  $\square$

