    &=\angle EBE_{AB}+\angle ECE_{CD}
    &=(90^\circ-\angle EAE_{AB})+(90^\circ-\angle EDE_{CD})
    &=180^\circ-(\angle EAE_{AB}+\angle EDE_{CD})
    &=180^\circ-(\angle EE_{DA}E_{AB}+\angle EE_{DA}E_{CD})
    &=180^\circ-\angle E_{AB}E_{DA}E_{CD}.
\end{align*}
So  $E_{AB}E_{BC}E_{CD}E_{DA}$  is cyclic as well, and taking a homothety at  $E$  with scale factor  $2$  finishes.  $\square$

